{"availability":"available","full":"Luanafrtd/remote-job-dashboard","name":"remote-job-dashboard","description":"A single place for a job seeker to track applications and follow-ups instead of a spreadsheet. Front-end skill demo built with Next.js 15, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-16T15:28:14Z","updated":"2026-08-22T13:44:07Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://remote-job-dashboard.vercel.app","topics":["accessibility","dashboard","nextjs","portfolio-project","react","tailwindcss","typescript","vercel"],"demo":"https://remote-job-dashboard.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:12.435Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:12.435Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:12.435Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:02:12.435Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A single place for a job seeker to track every application and follow-up, instead of a spreadsheet that's always a little out of date. Built with Next.js 15 (App Router), TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS v4 as a front-end skill demo: authentication UI backed by a real middleware route guard, streaming server components with Suspense skeletons, interactive charts, and a full profile/settings experience.","Applying to a dozen roles across a dozen browser tabs makes it easy to lose track of which company you already followed up with, and a spreadsheet only stays accurate for as long as someone remembers to update it. Remote Job Dashboard is built for exactly that: a single, fast place to see every application, its status, and what needs a follow-up next. This repo is the front end of that idea, built to demonstrate how a production Next.js App Router app is actually put together: a protected dashboard behind real middleware, streaming server components with Suspense skeletons, a full auth flow,…"],"features":["Protected dashboard: middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated visitors to /login?from= and sends authenticated visitors away from the auth pages, mirroring how a real app gates its routes","Streaming dashboard: each dashboard section (metrics, trend chart, pipeline chart, category chart, recent applications) is its own async server component wrapped in , so slow sections don't block fast ones, with…","Authentication UI: login and register pages with client-side validation, password visibility toggle, and a split-screen layout","Sidebar navigation: responsive, collapses into a mobile drawer (with focus-safe Escape-to-close and scroll lock), active-route highlighting","Profile page: editable personal info, skills, and activity summary"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Luanafrtd/remote-job-dashboard/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e860dae78a51fa8e43ac15ed9329fbf5ae107d1afd0f10ed926821afccfc46c9","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:12.538Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:12.538Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A single place for a job seeker to track every application and follow-up, instead of a spreadsheet that's always a little out of date. Built with Next.js 15 (App Router), TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS v4 as a front-end skill demo: authentication UI backed by a real middleware route guard, streaming server components with Suspense skeletons, interactive charts, and a full profile/settings experience.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Luanafrtd/remote-job-dashboard/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Applying to a dozen roles across a dozen browser tabs makes it easy to lose track of which company you already followed up with, and a spreadsheet only stays accurate for as long as someone remembers to update it. Remote Job Dashboard is built for exactly that: a single, fast place to see every application, its status, and what needs a follow-up next. This repo is the front…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Luanafrtd/remote-job-dashboard/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"The root URL redirects to /login; sign in with any non-empty email/password, or use Continue as guest, to reach the protected dashboard (there's no real backend, so any input works).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Luanafrtd/remote-job-dashboard/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Protected dashboard: middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated visitors to /login?from= and sends authenticated visitors away from the auth pages, mirroring how a real app gates its routes","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Luanafrtd/remote-job-dashboard/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"The architecture is streaming-ready without paying a runtime cost for data that doesn't need it.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Luanafrtd/remote-job-dashboard/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"e860dae78a51fa8e43ac15ed9329fbf5ae107d1afd0f10ed926821afccfc46c9","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Luanafrtd/remote-job-dashboard/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:12.539Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-22T13:44:07Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Luanafrtd/remote-job-dashboard/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:12.540Z","hash":"e860dae78a51fa8e43ac15ed9329fbf5ae107d1afd0f10ed926821afccfc46c9","originalBytes":19009,"storedBytes":19009,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["dashboard","real","run","auth","npm","src","login","route","server","components","data","production","app","build","charts","every","lib","profile","settings","chart","layout","metadata","next","next.js","page","protected","sidebar","url","vercel","what","backend","component","dark","mock","playwright","root","routes","see","text","any","async","before","boundaries","built","client","cookie","demo","full","generated","job","redirects","screenshots","session","test","theme","there","they","typescript","already","api.